## 5. Data Management

### 5.1 Data Availability
| Test Type | Data Source | Environment | Data Type | Data Volume | Comments |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Automation, Functional | Mocked Jira API, credential matrix | Staging | Valid/invalid tokens | Low | Simulate 401/200 responses |

---

## 6. Test Schedule / Milestone
- Test script development: 2 days (1 QA automation engineer)
- Environment setup and credential matrix: 1 day (DevOps support)
- Test execution: 2 days (QA)
- Results analysis and reporting: 1 day (QA lead)
- Total estimated duration: 6 working days

---

## 7. Assumptions
- Staging environment supports toggling authentication states.
- Test data (credentials) can be safely injected and revoked.
- All tools (PyTest, Playwright, JMeter, OWASP ZAP, tcconfig) are available and licensed.
- DevOps and QA resources are available as scheduled.

---

## 8. Risks & Mitigations
| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Likelihood | Mitigation Action | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| R1 | Staging environment cannot simulate all authentication states | High | Medium | Use mock proxy to inject 401 responses | QA Lead |
| R2 | Credential matrix not representative of production | Medium | Medium | Review with Jira admin, use real revoked/expired tokens | QA Lead |
| R3 | Tooling (e.g., OWASP ZAP, JMeter) not available or misconfigured | Medium | Low | Pre-validate toolchain, provide fallback scripts | DevOps |
| R4 | Timeline slippage due to resource contention | Medium | Medium | Pre-allocate QA/DevOps, escalate early | Project Manager |
| R5 | API rate limiting or lockout during negative testing | Low | Medium | Throttle test execution, coordinate with Jira admin | QA Lead |

